next_action:
  id: AR-4-INITIAL-MODEL
  description_es: Iniciar el Modelo de Reconstrucción definiendo semántica, clases, requisitos de evidencia, resultados parciales/ambiguos/imposibles y separación respecto de Binding y autoridad.
  description_en: Start the Reconstruction Model by defining semantics, classes, evidence requirements, partial/ambiguous/impossible outcomes, and separation from Binding and authority.
  decision_target: AR-4 INITIAL MODEL

ar_4_initial_questions:
  - what reconstruction means
  - reconstruction classes
  - required information/evidence by class
  - partial reconstruction semantics
  - ambiguous reconstruction semantics
  - impossible reconstruction semantics
  - provenance preservation
  - degradation propagation
  - reconstruction vs authorization
  - reconstruction vs Binding
  - reconstructed equivalence/fidelity conditions
  - neutral non-KOS applicability

phase_2_plan:
  - AR-4 Reconstruction Model
  - AR-5 KSCL Decomposition
  - Gate B

reopen_gate_a_if:
  - AR-4 requires incompatible reconstruction ownership transfer into AR-3
  - reconstruction requires fundamental AR-2 semantic change
  - AR-1 cannot express required property transitions
  - circular authority/dependency appears
  - conceptual non-KOS neutrality fails
  - encoding or transport becomes inseparable from Phase I semantic core

reentry_rule:
  - verify actual Git HEAD before development
  - reconcile CURRENT.kscl against later commits/documents
  - do not infer authority from this record

assertions:
  - CURRENT.kscl is mutable continuity state
  - checkpoint is historical snapshot
  - KSCL continuity != architectural authority
  - KSCL reconstruction != proof
  - Gate A PASS != KOS-Lab integration authorization
